  "hashFunction": "Not identified. Tried against the invented vectors, on the path with `.lock`, without it, and with a few prefixes: MD5, truncated SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512, BLAKE2b, BLAKE2s, BLAKE3 and the xxHash 128-bit and paired 64-bit forms, 112 combinations with no match. So whether a Host can compute this name without running Oh My Pi's code is open.",
  "observed": "The Terminal's process holds no @omp-file-lock socket at the prompt. It holds exactly one from the same sample the file appears in, through the time the file is not open, and `/new` replaces it with another. Inside that window the program's own function refused the lease for the session id in the file's name and granted it for an unrelated id. After the process ended, that function bound the very names the process had held, for both ids in both runs. The same id and home give the same name, and another home gives another, so the name is decided by the owners directory and the session id, one lock to one session."
